  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge continues to track toward the eastern CONUS \nearly next week. Long-range models suggest the ridge axis meanders \neast of our region through much of the upcoming week. Given a \nrelatively stagnant weather pattern, conditions through the Long \nTerm period look cookie-cutter. Each afternoon shall feature \nhighs ranging within the upper 90s to low 100s. Triple digit heat \nwill tend to favor portions of the northeastern Permian Basin and\nthose in and around the river valleys. Lows each night cool into \nthe 60s across the higher elevations, with low to mid 70s for \nalmost everywhere else. Most of the region is expected to remain \ndry through the extended period. However, isolated showers and \nstorms may develop in and near the higher terrain west of the \nPecos most afternoons. These driven by the combination of upslope \nflow and transient disturbances along the southern edge of the \nridge.",
